tring is invalid.\n\n`encode_key(key)` returns the canonical text for a key.  The top-level key has\ndepth 1; every level of nesting increases the depth by 1; encoding any value at\na depth greater than `MAX_KEY_DEPTH` raises `ValueError`.  Supported types, in\nthis precedence order:\n\n* `None`              -> `\"n:\"`\n* `bool`              -> `\"b:true\"` / `\"b:false\"` (checked before `int`)\n* `int`               -> `\"i:\"` + decimal digits, e.g. `\"i:-7\"`\n* `float`             -> `\"f:\"` + `repr(value)`; `-0.0` is normalised to `0.0`\n                         first; non-finite floats raise `ValueError`\n* `str`               -> `\"s:\"` + escaped text\n* `bytes`             -> `\"x:\"` + `value.hex()`\n* `list` / `tuple`    -> `\"l:[\"` + items joined with `\"|\"` + `\"]\"`; lists and\n                         tuples with equal items encode identically\n* `dict`              -> `\"d:{\"` + pairs joined with `\"|\"` + `\"}\"`, where each\n                         pair is `encode_key(name) + \"=\" + encode_key(value)`\n                         and pairs are ordered by ascending `sorted()` order of\n                         the raw string names.  Every dict key must be a `str`,\n                         otherwise `TypeError`.  Names and values are encoded at\n                         depth+1.\n* anything else       -> `TypeError`\n\nEscaping for `str` replaces, in this order, `\\` with `\\\\`, `|` with `\\p`, and\n`=` with `\\e`.  Nothing else is escaped.\n\n`canonical_key(namespace, key)` returns `check_namespace(namespace) + \"/\" +\nencode_key(key)`.\n\n=====================================================================\n3. `nscache/core.py` - the cache\n=====================================================================\n\n`FRESH = \"fresh\"` and `STALE = \"stale\"` are module constants.\n\n`CacheEntry` is a `NamedTuple` with exactly the fields, in this order:\n`namespace`, `canonical`, `value`, `stored_at`, `expires_at`, `state`.\n\n`NamespacedCache