ze` is `len(self)`.  Mutating a returned dict must never affect the cache\n  or a later `stats()` call.\n\n`get`, `get_entry`, `put` and `keys` all validate their namespace and key\nthrough `canonical_key`, so invalid namespaces and unsupported key types raise\nbefore anything else happens.\n\n=====================================================================\n4. `nscache/snapshot.py` and snapshot/restore\n=====================================================================\n\n`SNAPSHOT_VERSION` is the integer `2`.\n\n`build_snapshot(created_at, capacity, ttl, stale_ttl, entries)` returns a new\ndict with exactly the keys `version` (`SNAPSHOT_VERSION`), `created_at`\n(validated with `check_real`), `capacity`, `ttl`, `stale_ttl` and `entries`,\nwhere `entries` is a new list holding a shallow copy (`dict(entry)`) of each\nsupplied entry mapping.\n\n`parse_snapshot(data)` validates and returns a `(created_at, records)` pair,\nwhere `records` is a list of new dicts with the keys `canonical`, `namespace`,\n`value`, `stored_at`, `expires_at` in the original order.  Validation happens in\nthis order:\n\n1. `data` must be a `dict`, else `TypeError`.\n2. Any of `version`, `created_at`, `capacity`, `ttl`, `stale_ttl`, `entries`\n   missing -> `ValueError`.\n3. `version` must be the `int` `2` (a `bool` or any other value, including the\n   string `\"2\"` or the integer `1`) -> `ValueError`.\n4. `created_at` is validated with `check_real`.\n5. `entries` must be a `list`, else `TypeError`.\n6. Each entry must be a `dict` (`TypeError`), must contain all five entry fields\n   (`ValueError`), must have `str` `canonical` and `namespace` (`TypeError`),\n   and its `stored_at`/`expires_at` are validated with `check_real`.\n\n`NamespacedCache.snapshot()` first calls `purge_expired()`, then returns\n`build_snapshot(now, self.capacity, self.ttl, self.stale_ttl, entries)` where\n`entries` lists every remaining record (FRESH and STALE) least recently used\nfirst, each as a mapping with